    text: '---\nid: how-engagements-start\ntitle: How an engagement with Vitalos starts\ntype: guide\nurl: /how-we-work\nstatus: published\nowner: Temitope Agbola\nreview_date: 2027-01-15\n---\n\nYou can start in three ways: with consulting, with a discovery or assessment, or by going straight to engineering when the requirements are already clear.\n\n## When discovery comes first\n\nFor complex, uncertain or high-risk work, discovery comes first. Discovery exists to reduce uncertainty before a large commitment: it is the right start when the problem is unclear, several teams or systems are affected, legacy behaviour is poorly understood, or data and AI readiness are unknown.\n\n## How we work through an engagement\n\nWe assess, architect, engineer and operate. A recommendation only matters if it can be engineered, released and run safely, so the same team stays connected from advice to production.\n\n## Taking the first step\n\nUse "Talk to Vitalos" on the website, or ask Relay for a person. Describe the problem rather than the technology; a person from the team will suggest the right starting point.\n',
